    "updated_at": "2026-03-18T05:08:38Z",
    "body": "I was looking at the spec a a bit, and I'm wondering about the expected behavior here.\n\nShould we invoke [\"Fail the WebSocket connection\"](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6455#section-7.1.7), or should we follow the [make disappear](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#make-disappear) steps in [unloading-document-cleanup-steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#unloading-document-cleanup-steps)? If we follow the make disappear steps, `onerror` would only fire for the CONNECTING state. \n\nI'd love to know what the recommended approach is here, or hear any thoughts on this.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
