    "created_at": "2026-04-09T10:56:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T10:56:47Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the input! It seems to make sense that, as originally proposed, the user agent should fire an error event before close, with wasClean set to false.\n\nWe are planning to start experimenting with this in Chromium to confirm the performance benefits and web compatibility. While it's still too early to merge, I've opened a draft [PR](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12349) to discuss the spec integration. The approach is to check the salvageable state during unloading and call the \"fail the websocket connection\" (I thnk some more changes are needed as we cannot directly link [it](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6455#section-7.1.7) from the HTML spec).\n\nDoes this look like a reasonable way to hook this into the specs?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
